From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shu Zhao <shuzhao.cs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:32:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat: --fp32-lm-head scores the policy with chunked fp32
 logits

--sglang-enable-fp32-lm-head samples from fp32 logits, while Megatron's
output layer rounds the trainer's logits to bf16, so the trainer scores a
different distribution than the engines sampled. With --fp32-lm-head the
model returns its final hidden states through Megatron's output_processor
hook, and get_log_probs_and_entropy computes each response's log-probs from
fp32 logits (bf16 hidden states x bf16 output weight, fp32 accumulation and
output), --log-probs-chunk-size tokens at a time; the backward recomputes
each chunk's logits and runs its matmuls in fp32 storage with TF32 math.
No [tokens, vocab] logits of the whole micro-batch exist (fp32 logits of a
69,632-token micro-batch over a 248,320-token vocabulary would be 69 GB).
The entropy, when asked, is observed only (--entropy-coef 0). Megatron with
TP 1 and CP 1.
